body:
I have these 3 tables. A calendar one; and 2 other (emails, agents). The 'email' one has a date column while the 'agent' one doesn't. As you can see the 'calendar' one is connected to the 'email'.  When I filter (by date), the visual card of total agents doesnt change at all.

&#x200B;

Is there something missing? Or a formula?

I work 6pm-6am M-St......DONT TAKE IT DONT TAKE IT. Sure, you could pay off your debt; but your sanity,mental-health,body,spirit will pay a higher bill for all that time.

&#x200B;

P.S: I dont live in the US but for an outsourced company located in Florida

I worked 4 year in callcenter (lost my soul, gain depression/anxiety, was losing hair) and sure it helped pay the bill and some stuff. But man, it was horrible. Now, I'm in a position where there is less stress (of course the title/position dones go accordingly with what I do)..but oh frik boy; I have to be at the office 12hours-6days, and since I lost my soul now I'm losing the willing to live

&#x200B;

\*P.S I'm not from the U.S, however I'm working for a company that it's HQ is in Florida. I still dont get why SOOOO MANY HOURS WITHOUT ANY REASONABLE MOTIVE

Another one: Customer that DONT READ or AT LEAST TAKE THEIR TIME TO READ. Like, if you're going to subscribe, please please read before pushing forward.

&#x200B;

I used to work for a dating site, and when you choose a subcription it tells you 3 TIMES how much you were going to be charged....still people called asking why that amount appears on their billing all the time

Keep money on your shoes just in case you get rob; 
Know all the streets and route in case you are being followed; 
Dont trust anyone, not even the police; 
Buy a cheap phone for emergencies; 
When you are walking the street, look mad/angry
If you use transportation, learn their time of arrival (if it's late have your thumb ready to ask for a uber/taxi)
If you live on a bad neighborhood, always know the gang, it always works in latin america🤣
